I was horrified with the state of the documentation for Conquer.
So, wanting to learn nroff/troff anyway, I embarked on converting
this ugly document into a thing of beauty.  (I also don't have
much to do this summer  :-)  )

All six files (txt[0-5]) now have tbl and *roff -ms macro formatting.
Because most terminals don't handle tbl output very well, these
are really only good for high quality troff (pstroff, psroff, thack,
etc) output.  My final copies were printed with pstroff on a 
Laser Writer and look 100 times better.

But looks aren't everything.  The documents were most helped by
converting the hand formatted tables into tbl with boxes and
nifty columns.  Alas, the rest of the docs still suffer from
poor prose, grammar, and inconsistencies.  Items that blatantly
screamed "ugly", I retrofitted into readability but most of
it would fail any writing test.

(BTW, that was a minor flame.  Burners off.)

I am unsure how to distribute these, so please send me mail
with requests or suggestions.

Hopefully, the authors will see the light and format all future
documenation in this manner.  I suggest separate on-line and
off-line docs (getting something readable from my docs just
requires removing some tbl line drawing).

